WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.022
Use this lesson actively. Read the idea first and make a prediction before running any code.

00:00:06.022 --> 00:00:09.242
When a Python cell is available, click Run, inspect the output,

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:13.632
and then change one small value or condition.

00:00:13.632 --> 00:00:16.432
Run it again and explain what changed.

00:00:16.432 --> 00:00:22.577
This predict, run, modify, and explain cycle is more useful than copying a finished example.

00:00:22.577 --> 00:00:26.347
Machine learning is a workflow rather than a single fit command.

00:00:26.347 --> 00:00:31.837
Keep training information separate from evaluation data, compare against a baseline,

00:00:31.837 --> 00:00:36.302
and interpret model performance in the context of the real prediction problem.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:42.062
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:42.062 --> 00:00:47.480
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
